@page "/test/table-variants"
@model OperaLegacyLab.Web.Pages.Test.TableVariantsModel
@using OperaLegacyLab.Web.Infrastructure
@{
    var code = Model.Lab.Code;
}
<h1>Table cell sizing variants test</h1>
<p>Five small 12x12 checkerboards below (numbered 2-6 - Variant 1 was removed, it turned out to render
stretched even in a desktop browser, so it wasn't telling us anything about old-phone rendering), each
built with a different combination of table-sizing techniques. Each SHOULD be a square, exactly 72x72
pixels. If a technique doesn't keep a &lt;td&gt; at its declared height, the checkerboard comes out as a
tall thin rectangle instead - look at each one and note, in the form at the bottom, which numbers looked
like a square and which looked stretched.</p>
<p><font size="1">Variant 2 is the exact technique the real QR code pages (<a href="@Markup.U("/test/qr-table", code)">/test/qr-table</a>)
already use today - if it looks stretched here too, that confirms this page is reproducing the same bug,
not a different one.</font></p>

@foreach (var (spec, html) in Model.Variants)
{
    <hr>
    <h2>@spec.Label</h2>
    <p><font size="1">@spec.Description</font></p>
    @Html.Raw(html)
}

<hr>
@Html.Raw(SelfReport.Form(Model.Lab.Code,
    "Which variant numbers (2-6) looked like a correct square, and which looked stretched? Write the numbers in the notes box below (e.g. \"2,4 stretched - 3,5,6 square\")."))

<p><a href="@Markup.U("/test/qr-table", code)">Back to the real QR (table) test</a></p>
